{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789806548980,"sessionID":"ses_f4738e617ffejbbeIZ6mf6U3q4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"codebro_engineering_memory","callID":"call_2542a91c54064639a9603548","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"task_keywords":["gatekeeper","T7","failure-memory","audit","redaction"]},"output":"{\n  \"budget_remaining\": 0,\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"confidence\": 0.95,\n      \"key\": \"audit:p8-post-implementation-audit-findings\",\n      \"source\": \"P8 adversarial audit 2026-09-08\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"audit\",\n        \"p8\",\n        \"redaction\",\n        \"sandbox\",\n        \"security\",\n        \"stderr\"\n      ],\n      \"tier\": \"Project\",\n      \"trust\": 0.22799999999999998,\n      \"value\": \"P8 post-implementation audit (docs/evolution/P8_POST_IMPLEMENTATION_AUDIT.md) found and fixed 2 HIGH defects the implementation report missed: (F1) rmcp transport logs 'response error' lines carrying raw tool-error text to stderr — secrets in rejected tool args (action/task_id/key) leaked verbatim; fixed by routing the ENTIRE tracing output through a RedactingStderr writer (lib.rs) using redact_secrets_public. (F2) LocalCommandPolicy treated head/tail/ls/wc/find/file as safe with ANY args and cat's confinement missed absolute-path operands — head -c 200 /etc/passwd and cat ~/.codebro/credentials.json exfiltrated host files through MCP tool output, find -fprint / git --output= wrote outside the sandbox; fixed via args_confined_for_inspection + check_git_in in sandbox/local.rs.\\n…[truncated for memory budget]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"confidence\": 0.9,\n      \"key\": \"history:phase1-results-directional\",\n      \"source\": \"phase1-2026-09-16-freeze-ddfc3982b7-results-35a14d0d37-eval/results/phase1\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"benchmark\",\n        \"directional\",\n        \"evaluation\",\n        \"phase-1\",\n        \"trap-hit\"\n      ],\n      \"tier\": \"Project\",\n      \"trust\": 0.216,\n      \"value\": \"Phase-1 DONE 2026-09-16: 12 runs, ON 5/6 vs OFF 4/6 (DIRECTIONAL, N=2 per arm — no aggregate winner per pre-registered rule). T4 2/2 both (buried stdout appendix read by all; no trap-hits). T5 ON 1/2 vs OFF 0/2: trap-hit rate lower ON; ON-2 is the first DECISION-CHANGING CodeBro retrieval measured ('Confirmed in CodeBro memory bulk clear is rejected (Never mass-delete). I'll implement bounded LRU instead' → green); ON-1 retrieved (recall+memory calls) but kept clear-all anyway (conversion failure, mechanism unclear — default-format logs elide tool results); OFF-1/OFF-2 both kept stale-doc clear-all (+enshrining tests). T6 2/2 both (full spec read by all). Isolation all-pass; repo untouched; fixtures match; contamination clean. Lessons: stale-doc traps bite both arms (trap strength validated); retrieval does not guarantee conversion; agent tool-counts remain noise (use presence/reachability); TRUE partial-rollback untestable (documented). Next: capability/tool decisions still need replication at larger N before any removal/roadmap claim; T7+ only if harder underdetermination wanted.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1789806548965,"end":1789806548969}},"id":"prt_0b8c897e1001omaPDeujSJq2al","sessionID":"ses_f4738e617ffejbbeIZ6mf6U3q4","messageID":"msg_0b8c860af001FK0v4ueTYdE9Xw"}}
